        "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23442649",
        "A three-point counterexample to a random lattice discrepancy comparison \u2014 Alec Kriebel, v1.0.0 (2026-10-17). Problem30000052 / OWR-723-005; Novak reporting joint work with Hinrichs, OWR13/2004 p.698. Full negative answer to the universal expected normalized anchored p-th-power comparison for independent continuous uniform generator and shift: n=3, d=1, p=4 has lattice 19/1620 > iid 4/405, gap 1/540 and ratio 19/16. Three is the minimal point count; whole laws equal at n\u22642, second moments equal all n,d. Empty-tail bound 2/[105(n-1)] reverses iid for all n\u22654 in d=1. Four-page note, original full proof, seven exact verification programs. Explicit overlap with Alper Ferudun14Oct2026 DOI10.5281/zenodo.23372668 (same values and broader results) prominently credited. Source PR GitHub creation record10Oct; present note17Oct; historical public visibility/first discovery/publication uncertified; no causal attribution or first-priority claim. Bounded literature review with inaccessible full/final bodies and incomplete citation coverage. Extensive AI assistance; unrefereed, no external human peer review/formal certification. Two successive fresh independent whole-package reviews passed the identical release without unresolved issues. https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1135 Published record: https://zenodo.org/records/23442649"
